# ml_peg/app/data is the Dash assets folder, so it holds two unrelated things:
# the generated benchmark tree (never committed) and the hand-authored front-end
# assets. The latter all live in ui/, so a single exception covers them and the
# data tarball unpacks alongside rather than on top of tracked files.
# The `**` line matters: un-ignoring the directory only lets git descend into it,
# and the files inside would still match the *.json/*.svg/*.csv rules above.
ml_peg/app/data/*
!ml_peg/app/data/ui/
!ml_peg/app/data/ui/**
# Generated by ml_peg/models/element_coverage, but committed: the element filter
# reads it at import time (filters.py).
!ml_peg/app/data/element_coverage.json
# The committed app fixture; without this the *.json/*.xyz rules above exclude
# it. Scoped to app/ on purpose — the rest of tests/data holds locally generated
# baselines (test_high_pressure_relaxation_regression writes its own on first
# run) that should stay ignored.
!tests/data/app/**
certs/
# The tests no longer download this, but the README and user guide still tell
# developers to unpack it here to run the app against real data.
data.tar.gz
scratchpad/
